From: PAPPL OHOS port
Subject: [PATCH] Do not double-detach already detached threads

papplSystemRun() creates the raw-socket and USB gadget threads with
pthread_attr_setdetachstate(PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED) and then calls
pthread_detach() on them again. glibc tolerates the redundant call
(returning EINVAL), but on musl-based systems (OHOS) the second
pthread_detach() dereferences invalid thread state and segfaults the
process. Drop the redundant calls; the threads are already detached.

---
--- a/pappl/system.c
+++ b/pappl/system.c
@@ -564,8 +564,8 @@
       }
       else
       {
-	// Detach the main thread from the raw thread to prevent hangs...
-	pthread_detach(tid);
+	// Note: the thread is already created detached (tattr above);
+	// calling pthread_detach() again crashes on musl-based systems...
 
         _papplRWLockRead(printer);
 	while (!printer->raw_active)
@@ -598,8 +598,8 @@
     }
     else
     {
-      // Detach the main thread from the USB thread to prevent hangs...
-      pthread_detach(tid);
+      // Note: the thread is already created detached (tattr above);
+      // calling pthread_detach() again crashes on musl-based systems...
 
       _papplRWLockRead(printer);
       while (!printer->usb_active)
